#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:56
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:58
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmobiletools; is a program that lets you manage mobile phones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It handles full SMS control, dialing calls, phonebook, and phone status "
"monitoring. It's also integrated with the &kde; environment, so it can be "
"embeded in &kontact;, or import/export from and to &kaddressbook;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:61
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmobiletools; is completely modular: the main program can load so called "
"\"Engines\" which can support different range of devices. Each engine also "
"has a set of wizard pages, so that the user is guided in adding new devices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:64
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>AT Engine</acronym> has been tested on Motorola, Nokia, Siemens, "
"Sony Ericsson and LG mobile phones. Anyway each AT Command compliant device "
"should be well supported. It allows the user to upload and download the "
"phonebook, view SMS stored on the phone, and write new ones. It also can "
"dial numbers and display phone parameters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:67
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<acronym>Gammu Engine</acronym> uses <ulink url=\"http://www.gammu."
"org\">Gammu</ulink> as backend to connect to the mobile phone, and so the "
"list of supported phones can be found in the project homepage (<ulink "
"url=\"http://www.gammu.org/wiki/index.php?title=Phones:Support\"></ulink> or "
"<ulink url=\"http://cihar.com/gammu/phonedb/\"></ulink>). It has almost the "
"same features than the AT Engine, and even something more, but it is younger "
"and less tested. It also supports a smaller list of mobile phones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmobiletools; homepage can be found on <ulink url=\"http://www.kmobiletools."
"org\"></ulink>. There you will find user documentation, a support forum and "
"contact information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Getting Started"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This chapter is just a short introduction to &kmobiletools; as well as its "
"usage so you can start using it right away. More information on using "
"&kmobiletools; can be found in the <link linkend=\"using-"
"kmobiletools\">Using &kmobiletools;</link> section."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When starting &kmobiletools; for the first time, you will see the welcome "
"homepage."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:83 index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kmobiletools; main window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wizard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the <guilabel>Add new mobile phone device</guilabel> link will "
"launch a wizard that will help you in configuring &kmobiletools; to use your "
"mobile phone."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kmobiletools; new device wizard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:95
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Mobile Phone Name</guilabel> entry will allow you to choose a "
"friendly name to be displayed in &kmobiletools; for your phone. The field "
"below instead is used to choose the engine that will manage your mobile "
"phone. The next wizard pages will be different for each engine."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:98
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using &kmobiletools;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This Chapter will show you &kmobiletools; usage in the most common tasks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:105
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kmobiletools; Main Window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main window will show you a list of configured phones. It will display "
"also their current status:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not Loaded: the engine relative to this mobile phone is not loaded."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "Not Connected: the engine is loaded, but the phone is not found."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Connected: the engine is loaded, and the phone was found as manageable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Mobile Phone HomePage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Mobile Phone Homepage will show you some useful information about your "
"mobile phone, like the number of messages, contacts, and a brief summary of "
"the calendar. In the status bar you will also see your network operator "
"(when supported), and the level of battery and network signal, plus a visual "
"representation of currently executing tasks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking on the <guilabel>Phone details</guilabel> link will also show you "
"more advanced information, like phone manufacturer and model or the IMEI "
"code."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kmobiletools; device homepage"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid "Phonebook Management"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kmobiletools; Phonebook Management page contains a list of entries and a "
"html-like page showing details. While the <guilabel>Phone Contacts</"
"guilabel> tab will show you contacts from the current mobile phone, the "
"<guilabel>Other Contacts</guilabel> tab contains items from other devices, "
"and &kaddressbook;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking an entry will automatically update the details page. In the details "
"page, at the bottom row there will be a list of tasks to handle contacts, "
"creating new items, removing and modifying current ones. You can also right "
"click a contact in the list, and selecting multiple items will work too, "
"when appropriate."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:132 index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kmobiletools; phonebook management page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Adding new contacts is easy! You just need to click the <guilabel>Add new</"
"guilabel> link, then choose the name to assign to this contact in the new "
"dialog window appearing. Remember also to add phone numbers entering it in "
"the <guilabel>Phone numbers</guilabel> text box and clicking the "
"<guilabel>Add</guilabel> button after having selected the proper number type "
"in the combo box above that button. You can also choose where you want to "
"save the new contact."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:146
#, no-c-format
msgid "Short Text Messages Management"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:147
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The SMS Page is similar to a mail application like &kmail;. The left list "
"shows the count of messages and their position, while the right one shows "
"the sender number (or the name, if it is found in the phonebook), the date "
"of the message and the subject. Finally, the page at down will show the "
"message text, plus some actions allowing you to remove messages, or write a "
"new one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:148 index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here's a screenshot of &kmobiletools; sms list page"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Clicking the <guilabel>Write New</guilabel> link will pop up a simple dialog "
"window that will guide you in writing a new SMS Message. Just remember to "
"add a recipient first, by both writing the number in the text box or picking "
"it from the phonebook clicking the <guilabel>Browse</guilabel> button, and "
"then the <guilabel>Add</guilabel> button. You will now need to write the "
"message itself in the box below, and then clicking one of the "
"<guilabel>Send</guilabel> or <guilabel>Store</guilabel> buttons."
msgstr ""

